# Firmware modules

This directory contains the firmware's reusable core and hardware-abstraction modules. Application screens are implemented separately in `src/Apps/`.

## Core

`Core/` defines the common app lifecycle and manages screen changes, button-event routing, inactivity warnings, and sleep behavior.

## Hardware abstraction layer

`HAL/` provides the interfaces used by the app screens to work with device hardware and storage:

- `DisplayController` initializes the e-paper panel and draws text and pages.
- `InputController` reads the four buttons and forwards click and long-press events.
- `StorageManager` accesses LittleFS files and saves bookmarks and user settings.
- `BookParser` reads book text in chunks and tracks the current file offset.

Keep hardware-specific behavior in `HAL/` and shared app lifecycle or routing behavior in `Core/`. Include the module headers from application code as needed.
